Afterwards, I walked over to the city's large museum.
It was about the famous author Hans Christian Andersen.
I bought my ticket and went into the beautiful building.
The exhibition told about his life and his long journeys.
I looked at his old things in a large glass case.
He took his top hat with him everywhere.
The tall, black hat lay right there in front of me.
There lay also his paper and his old pen.
He used them when he wrote his fantastic fairy tales.
I read a long text on a white wall.
It was about the man behind my favorite fairy tale.
It was actually him who created the little mermaid.
I met her as a statue in Copenhagen back in February.
It was fun to see the author's own things now.
I took a few pictures of his large travel bag.
He apparently loved to visit new countries.
I bought a little book in the museum's shop at the end.
It contained all his best stories.
Now I feel that I know Danish culture a little better.
